# Build, CI and release

## CI cost policy
- No Claude job runs on GitHub Actions.
- Every workflow uses `on: workflow_dispatch` only. Never add `push`, `pull_request`, `pull_request_target`, `schedule`,
  `issue_comment` or any other automatic trigger, even "just for main".
- `tests.yml` is the only workflow. Do not add matrices, caches or extra jobs unless a plan asks for it.
- Never print or echo secrets.

## Packaging and release
- Arch packaging lives in `packaging/arch/`. Program files install read-only under `/usr/lib/proton-drive-cli-sync/`; user data stays in `~/.config/proton-drive-sync/` and `~/.proton-drive-sync/`.
- `CHANGELOG.md` follows Keep a Changelog with an `## [Unreleased]` section. Every user-visible behavior change adds an entry in the same PR.
- Tags, GitHub releases and AUR pushes are done by the user, never by the agent.
